23. Write Thread-Safe Classes in Java
    - Use synchronized methods or blocks
    - Make Fields Immutable
    - Use volatile keyword for shared variables
    - Use ReentrantLock for more flexibility and control over locking.
    - Use Atomic classes (e.g., AtomicInteger, AtomicReference) for simple thread-safe operations on single variables.
    - Use Concurrent Collections (e.g., ConcurrentHashMap, CopyOnWriteArrayList) for collections that need to be accessed by multiple threads.
    - Use Thread-Local Variables for Per-Thread Isolation
    - Use Executors and Shared State Wisely
    - Synchronize Only Critical Sections (Not Whole Methods)
    - Use ReadWriteLock for High Read-Low Write Scenarios
    - Avoid using static variables in multi-threaded environments unless they are properly synchronized.

