27. Hibernate Caching
    - First-Level Cache (Session Cache)
      • Enabled by default, stores entities within a session.
      • Automatically clears when the session is closed.
    - Second-Level Cache
      • Optional, shared across sessions.
      • Can use providers like Ehcache, Hazelcast, or Infinispan.
      • Configurable per entity or collection.
    - Query Cache
      • Caches query results to avoid re-executing the same query.
      • Requires second-level cache to be enabled.

